Answered in the block and cleared the tag.

**Weather:** November is the best month there — dry season starts, highs 83–88°F, ocean ~82–84°F, ~1 rainy day all month. First two weeks beat Thanksgiving week on price.

**Recs, ranked:**
1. **Four Seasons Punta Mita** — the pick. Complimentary Kids For All Seasons (5–12) *plus* Babies For All Seasons toddler programming added 2025, so both kids are covered; babysitting ~$18/hr. Two beaches, one calm and shallow specifically for little kids — the only genuinely toddler-safe water of the three. Aramara + Bahía hold up against the boutiques.
2. **Conrad Punta de Mita** — Turi Club from age 4 (comp per their site, $15/hr per third-party reviews — flagged to verify), waterslide/splash pad, Hilton points eligible. Beach runs rougher.
3. **Susurros del Corazón (Auberge)** — best food (Casamilpa) and design, but kids club is 5+ only and it's a surf beach. Halcie would be all nanny hours.

Skipped St. Regis (no kids club) and W (party atmosphere). Also noted Zeph turns 5 on Oct 13, so he clears every 5+ minimum by November.

